{"name":"Piano Mauve","hex":"#9e8996","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"piano","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive keyboard musical instrument, usually ranging over seven octaves, with white and black colored keys, played by pressing these keys, causing hammers to strike strings. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To play the piano.","To move (the fingers) up and down on, similar to the motions of a pianist playing the piano."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piano"},{"term":"mauve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich purple synthetic dye, which faded easily, briefly popular c. 1859‒1873 and now called mauveine.","A pale purple or violet colour, like the colour of the dye after it has faded."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mauve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Piano","blocks":[{"text":"A piano is a keyboard instrument that produces sound when its keys are pressed, activating an action mechanism where hammers strike strings. Modern pianos have a row of 88 black and white keys—with the exception of the Bosendörfer and Stuart & Sons pianos—and tuned to a chromatic scale in equal temperament. A musician who specializes in piano is called a pianist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG/330px-Steinway_Vienna_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano","wikidata":"Q5994"},{"title":"Mauve","blocks":[{"text":"Mauve is a pale purple color named after the mallow flower. The first use of the word mauve as a color was in 1796–1798 according to the Oxford English Dictionary, but its use seems to have been rare before 1859. Another name for the color is mallow, with the first recorded use of mallow as a color name in English in 1611."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wilde_Malve.JPG/330px-Wilde_Malve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauve","wikidata":"Q604079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/500px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg/500px-Piano_droit_Weinbach_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiano_droit_Weinbach_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/PianoRange.tif/lossy-page1-500px-PianoRange.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/PianoRange.tif/lossy-page1-500px-PianoRange.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APianoRange.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg/500px-CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg/1280px-CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyboardView.jpg/500px-CristoforiPiano1726LeipzigKeyb